005674562882632017,-4.0531076592742465e-06,0.0,-0.3505798578262329,0.0,0.0,-1.2498157024383545,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.024283356964588165,0.0,0.0,-2.9802276912960224e-06,-3.814689989667386e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-4.8993817472364753e-05,0.0,-0.2547468841075897,0.0,-4.434487345861271e-05,-0.009516824968159199,-1.4066597032069694e-05,-8.344646857949556e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-4.768370445162873e-07,0.0,0.0,-7.629103492945433e-05,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-2.0265558760002023e-06,-2.622600959512056e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,21095,400,1867,6484,3,702,4126,400,46,3,323,400,1867,14,1808,45157,12947,362,1459,374,26618,11882,504,279,14791,315,22756,400,1867,6484,12947,3555,374,279,18927,429,432,374,12128,311,400,46,3,1091,311,894,315,279,3040,17228,30,220,508,6405,921,2141,7,17,15,15,317,7633,54934,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,29621,7,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,29621,7,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,29621,4080,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,29621,21621,317,16119,1188,15,11,15,1106,1502,20912,46,3,44970,15,11,15,701,45,317,1502,20912,32,73315,4080,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,701,69214,1215,2383,20912,33,3,44970,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,701,3944,1215,2383,20912,34,3,44970,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,925,1215,2383,20912,35,73315,4080,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,16844,1215,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nRectangle $ABCD$ has center $O$ and $AB/AD=k$. A point is randomly chosen from the interior of rectangle $ABCD$. What is the probability that it is closer to $O$ than to any of the four vertices?  [asy]\nsize(200);\ndraw((-250,100)--(250,100)--(250,-100)--(-250,-100)--cycle);\ndot((0,0));\nlabel(\"$O$\",(0,0),N);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-250,100),NW); label(\"$B$\",(250,100),NE); label(\"$C$\",(250,-100),SE); label(\"$D$\",(-250,-100),SW);[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9d471b9d0d4db906a7bb3d095e3b8ed9d1b764676f46c6a91f7206ad7107f69d"},"seconds":37.793956995010376,"seed":23818479079703700,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to find the probability that a randomly chosen point in rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is closer to the center \\(O\\) than to any of the four vertices. We start by understanding the geometric configuration and the distances involved.\n\n1. **Identify the Coordinates and Ratios:**\n   Let's assume the coordinates of the vertices of rectangle \\(ABCD\\) are:\n   - \\(A = (-a, b)\\)\n   - \\(B = (a, b)\\)\n   - \\(C = (a, -b)\\)\n   - \\(D = (-a, -b)\\)\n   The center \\(O\\) of the rectangle is at \\((0, 0)\\).\n\n   Given that \\(AB/AD = k\\), we can assume \\(AB = 2a\\) and \\(AD = 2b\\), so \\(k = \\frac{2a}{2b} = \\frac{a}{b}\\).\n\n2. **Equidistant Points:**\n   The set of points that are equidistant from the center \\(O\\) and any vertex forms the perpendicular bisectors of the segments connecting \\(O\\) to the vertices. For example, the set of points equidistant from \\(O\\) and \\(A\\) is the line \\(x = -\\frac{a}{2}\\) and \\(y = \\frac{b}{2}\\).\n\n3. **Intersection of Bisectors:**\n   The lines that are the perpendicular bisectors of the segments from \\(O\\) to each vertex divide the rectangle into four regions. Each of these regions is a right triangle with the right angle at the center \\(O\\). The area of each of these triangles is \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of the area of the rectangle.\n\n4. **Area Calculation:**\n   The area of the rectangle is \\(2a \\times 2b = 4ab\\). The area of the region closer to the center \\(O\\) than to any of the vertices is the area of the square formed by the intersection of these bisectors, which is a square with side length \\(\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\) but scaled down to fit within the rectangle. This region is exactly a quarter of the rectangle.\n\n5. **Probability Calculation:**\n   The probability that a randomly chosen point is closer to \\(O\\) than to any of the vertices is the ratio of the area of the central region to the area of the rectangle. Since the central region is a quarter of the rectangle, the probability is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\text{Area of central region}}{\\text{Area of rectangle}} = \\frac{4ab/4}{4ab} = \\frac{1}{4}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly chosen point is closer to the center \\(O\\) than to any of the four vertices is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
